1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:11,000
What if two thirds of your factory
weren't allowed to write code?

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,500
This is Dark Factory, built in BAND.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,500
Three coding agents in one room.
Two of them cannot write code.

4
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:41,000
One human message starts it.
After this, nothing else is dispatched.

5
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:52,000
Before any code exists, the reviewer turns
the specification into 158 numbered items.

6
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:01,000
From the spec text only — never from the shipped
tests, which are a sample, not the graded set.

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,500
Then one seat corrects another.

8
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:15,500
The coordinator says: treat an empty body
as an empty object.

9
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The reviewer confirms — and rejects it as incomplete.
The stored body must be the empty object too,
or a legitimate retry reads as a key reuse.

10
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:33,000
Caught before a line of code was written.

11
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Nobody wired this handoff. Each seat reads the room
and mentions whoever holds the next role.

12
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:50,000
451 messages. 206 tool calls.
The code traces to the room.

13
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:57,500
147 tests. 147 passing —
run by us, not reported to us.

14
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:04,500
No floating point anywhere on the money path.
The reviewer wrote that rule before the code existed.

15
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:12,500
Three hours forty-nine. Eleven point seven
million tokens. Eleven dollars seventy.

16
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:20,000
We stopped the reviewer to save budget.

17
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:27,000
It missed two defects. We found them at the gate,
and the room log shows it.

18
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:34,500
Take BAND out and the factory doesn't degrade.
It disappears. The rejection has no channel.

19
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:40,000
Dark Factory. Built in BAND.
